  "skill_summaries": {
    "ultimate": "summon ghosts to bombard random enemies",
    "skill1": "HP sacrifice fires orb line, dealing area damage",
    "skill2": "sacrifice HP to deal damage; sacrifice summons for extra AoE damage",
    "skill3": "battle energy recovery from attacks grows with summon count",
    "skill4": "summon expiry converts remaining power to all-enemy damage",
    "skill5": "each hero defeat spawns an extra summon"
  },
  "play_overview": "[[Shemira]] is a short-ranged carry who **sacrifices HP to fuel damage**, firing orb lines and AoE bursts as her health falls. She **summons ghosts** that bombard random enemies, and each hero defeat adds another summon to widen pressure. Energy recovery from attacks scales with summon count, while expired summons convert their remaining power into an all-enemy burst. She needs **healing and protection** to cycle sacrifices long enough to reach her slow ultimate. She shines in long fights after her summon count grows, but early burst or denied sustain leaves her exposed.",
  "counter_overview": "[[Shemira]] is short-ranged and slow to ultimate; once ghosts and summon count build, random bombardment and HP-sacrifice loops take over. End the first life early with [[filter:backline-assassin]] like [[Ravion]] or [[Himmel]] when she is exposed, and use [[Lily May]] to catch the ultimate wind-up. Cut the HP recovery that funds sacrifices with [[filter:heal-inhibitor]] like [[Frieren]] or [[Gwyneth]], then race the summon loop with [[filter:energy-provider]] like [[Thador]] or [[Hugin]]."
